                            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+stack"} derived stack
                  %h2#theorems Theorems
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diaconescu%27s+theorem"} Diaconescu's theorem
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barr%27s+theorem"} Barr's theorem
                  %div
                    %p
                      %a{:href => "/nlab/edit/topos+theory+-+contents"} Edit this sidebar
          %h1#double_negation Double negation
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#in_logic"} In logic
              %li
                %a{:href => "#double_negation_locale"} In locale theory
              %li
                %a{:href => "#topology"} In topos theory
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#Properties"} Properties
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#Examples"} Examples
              %li
                %a{:href => "#InHigherToposTheory"} In higher topos theory
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_entries"} Related entries
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logic"} logic
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg{\neg{P}}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ¬
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negation"} negation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composite"} composite
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negation"} negation
            with itself. This is a
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closure+operator"} closure operator
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modality"} modality
            and as such a special case of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuation+monad"} continuation monad
          %p
            The
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+negation+translation"} double negation translation
            says that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proposition"} proposition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is provable in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+logic#classical_propositional_logic"} classical propositional logic
            precisely if its double negation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ¬
                  %mo ¬
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \not \not P
            is provable in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+logic"} constructive propositional logic
          %p
            The
            %em double negation topology
            closes morphisms under double negation (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DoubleNegationTopology"}
            below), and its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
            forms a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+topos"} boolean topos
            (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DoubleNegationSheavesFormBooleanTopos"}
            below). This notably serves to capture the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forcing"} forcing
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
            in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+topoi"}> classifying topoi
            ), see also remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RelationToForcing"}
            below.
          %h2#in_logic In logic
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+logic"} classical logic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+value"} truth value
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proposition"} proposition
            is itself. More abstractly, double negation is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity function
            on any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+algebra"} boolean algebra
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intuitionistic+logic"} intuitionistic logic
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mo ¬
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \Rightarrow \neg{\neg{P}}
            but not conversely. In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paraconsistent+logic"} paraconsistent logic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+algebra"} Heyting algebra
            (intuitionistic) or its dual (paraconsistent).
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+logic"} linear logic
          %h2#double_negation_locale In locale theory
          %p
            Even in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
            is a Heyting algebra but not a boolean algebra. Accordingly, double negation is usually not the identity on a frame. However, the operation of double negation is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nucleus"} nucleus
            on any frame.
          %p
            Thus, every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sublocale"} sublocale
            given by that nucleus, called the
            %strong double negation sublocale
            and denoted
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mo ¬
                        %mo ¬
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{\neg\neg}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+sublocale"} dense
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersection
            of all dense sublocales.
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spatial+locale"} spatial locale
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mo ¬
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L = L_{\neg\neg}
            if and only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+locale"} discrete locale
            on some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            of points. In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            must also have
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+equality"} decidable equality
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_X
              be the sheaf of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous
              (or
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+map"} smooth
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+map"} holomorphic
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+map"} regular
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              (or
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+scheme"} reduced scheme
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} pushforward
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} pullback
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_X
              to the smallest dense sublocale of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the sheaf of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meromorphic+functions"} meromorphic functions
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (i.e. sections over an open subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              are given by sections of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_X
              defined on some dense open subset
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \subseteq U
          %h2#topology In topos theory
          %p
            The notion of double negation sublocale may be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorified
            from locales to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is a(n
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+topos"} elementary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negation"} negation
            operator
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg \colon \Omega \to \Omega
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalisation"} internal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+algebra"} Heyting algebra
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              A topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mrow
                        %mo ¬
                        %mo ¬
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}_{\neg\neg}
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subtopos"} open subtopos
              is called
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊥
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bot
                  \-scattered
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/provability+logic"} provability logic
              (cf.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattered+topos"} scattered topos
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              The booleanization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mrow
                        %mo ¬
                        %mo ¬
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}_{\neg\neg}
              of a topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              has a close relative: the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/De+Morganization"} De Morganization
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}_m
          %h3#definition Definition
          #DoubleNegationTopology.num_defn
            %h6#definitionproposition Definition/Proposition
            %p
              %strong (double negation topology)
            %p The double negation morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\not \not \colon \Omega \to \Omega
            %p
              constitutes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere-Tierney+topology"} Lawvere-Tierney topology
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            %p
              This is called the
              = succeed "." do
                %strong double negation topology
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The topology axioms can be formulated in purely equational form, i.e., as equations between operations of the form
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^n \to \Omega
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Ω
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(-, \Omega)^n \to Hom(-, \Omega)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "Heyting+algebra#ToBooleanAlgebras"} here
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p#quiv
              In case of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mo ⇉
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\rightrightarrows}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo ¬
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg\neg
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closure+operator"} closure operator
              on subgraphs
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\subseteq Y
              amounts to adding to the edge set of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              all the edges in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              between vertices that are in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "-topology" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mo ¬
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg\neg
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quiv"} Quiv
          %h3#Properties Properties
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            be a(n
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+topos"} elementary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
          %p
          #DoubleNegationSheavesFormBooleanTopos.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              The sheaf topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mrow
                        %mo ¬
                        %mo ¬
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}_{\not \not} \hookrightarrow \mathcal{E}
              corresponding to the
              %a{:href => "#DoubleNegationTopology"} double negation topology
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DoubleNegationTopology"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+topos"} Boolean topos
          %p
            This appears for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+toposes"} sheaf toposes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            as
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MacLaneMoerdijk"} MacLane &amp; Moerdijk, theorem VI 3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+toposes"} elementary toposes
            as a special case of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone"} Johnstone, Lem. A4.5.21
          %p
            The following says that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
