            is the smallest subtopos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}_j
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ∅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset
            is a
            = succeed "-sheaf." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            as a generalized (topological) space becomes, as in the case of locales, rather remarkable.
          %p
          #smallest_dense_subtopos.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mrow
                        %mo ¬
                        %mo ¬
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}_{\not \not} \hookrightarrow \mathcal{E}
              is the smallest
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+subtopos"} dense subtopos
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Johnstone"}> Johnstone 2002, below Cor. A4.5.20
            , or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone77"} Johnstone 1977, p.140
          %p
            Another, slightly more general, way to state this is the following (cf.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BlassScedrov83"} Blass &amp; Scedrov 1983
            = succeed "," do
