          %h2#references References
          %p
            Informal exposition of double negation with an eye towards
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrej+Bauer"}> Andrej Bauer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://math.andrej.com/2008/08/13/intuitionistic-mathematics-for-physics/"} Intuitionistic mathematics for physics
          %p
            In
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
          %ul
            %li#Johnstone77
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                ,
                %em Topos Theory
                , Academic Press 1977 (Dover reprint 2014). (pp.139-140)
            %li#Johnstone
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sketches+of+an+Elephant"} Sketches of an Elephant
                    vols. I,II
            %li#MacLaneMoerdijk
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+Mac+Lane"}> Saunders Mac Lane
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sheaves+in+Geometry+and+Logic"} Sheaves in Geometry and Logic
                , Springer Heidelberg 1994. (chap. VI, in particular sec.VI.1)
          %p
            In
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Univalent+Foundations+Project"}> Univalent Foundations Project
              , section 3.4 of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+Type+Theory+--+Univalent+Foundations+of+Mathematics"} Homotopy Type Theory – Univalent Foundations of Mathematics
          %p
            Discussion in relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sharp+modality"} sharp modality
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Lawvere91
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F.+W.+Lawvere"}> F. W. Lawvere
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Some+Thoughts+on+the+Future+of+Category+Theory"} Some Thoughts on the Future of Category Theory
              , pp.1-13 in LNM
              %strong 1488
              Springer Heidelberg 1991.
          %p More detailed discussion of this is in
          %ul
            %li#LawvereMenni15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mat%C3%ADas+Menni"} Matías Menni
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Internal choice holds in the discrete part of any cohesive topos satisfying stable connected codiscreteness
                %strong 30
                no. 26 (2015) pp.909-932. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/30/26/30-26abs.html"}> abstract
                )
            %li#Menni18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mat%C3%ADas+Menni"}> Matías Menni
                ,
                %em The unity and identity of opposites between decidable objects and double-negation sheaves
                , JSL to appear. (
                %a{:href => "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18P2qsihtZG7_eCT5VdjvQ1I7T-U_S7y9/view"}> preprint
                )
          %p Other useful references include
          %ul
            %li#BlassScedrov83
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+Blass"}> Andreas Blass
                , Andrej Scedrov,
                %em Boolean Classifying Topoi
                , JPAA
                %strong 28
                (1983) pp.15-30.
            %li#Caramello09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Olivia+Caramello"}> Olivia Caramello
                ,
                %em De Morgan classifying toposes
                , Advances in Mathematics
                %strong 222
                no.6 (2009) pp.2117-2144. (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0808.1519"}> arXiv:0808.1519
                )
            %li#Caramello12a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Olivia+Caramello"}> Olivia Caramello
                ,
                %em Universal models and definability
                , Math. Proc. Cam. Phil. Soc. (2012) pp.279-302. (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0906.3061"}> arXiv:0906.3061
                )
            %li#Caramello12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Olivia+Caramello"}> Olivia Caramello
                ,
                %em Topologies for intermediate logics
                , arXiv:1205.2547 (2012). (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1205.2547"}> abstract
                )
            %li
              %p
                D. S. Mcnab,
                %em Some applications of double-negation sheafification
                , Proc. Edinburgh Math. Soc.
                %strong 20
                (1977) pp.279-285.
          .footnotes
            %hr/
            %ol
              %li#fn:1
                %p
                  %a{:href => "#Lawvere91"} Lawvere (1991)
                  says around p.8: “
                  %em>
                    The base in fact seems in examples to be determined by the given category of Being itself, either as the latter’s QD reflection with the extra localness condition supplying the right adjoint pure Becoming inclusion, or else (for example simplicial sets) as the double-negation sheaves with the extra essentialness condition supplying the left adjoint inclusion (in the latter case it is in
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aufhebung"} Hegelian fashion
                    always the smallest level for which both 0,1 are sheaves)“
                  \.
                  %a{:href => "#fnref:1", :rev => "footnote"} ↩
